{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509601-there-is-any-way-raw-to-become-a-3rd-generation-vampire","id":1509601,"title":"There is any way, RAW, to become a 3rd Generation vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T11:01:34-07:00","id":1509601,"title":"There is any way, RAW, to become a 3rd Generation vampire?","content":"I read both the supplements called Diablerie but they deal &quot;only&quot; with ancient Metuselah of the 4th generation.<br /> I've searched around the web but I have not found any statted Antediluvian... beside the Giovanni and even him only before he committed his final diablerie.<br /> <br /> There is anywhere an OFFICIAL ( no homebrew ) module or adventure that includes the chance to diablerize an Antediluvian, or to lower permanently the generation to the 3rd in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T11:33:42-07:00","id":1509604,"title":"","content":"<b>From Marduk's Throat</b> a level six ritual of Assamite Sorcery in <i>theory</i> ccould do it - Beckett's Jyhad Diary has the Laibon claim that the Assamite ritual was stolen from them. They say they have a version that lets their saintly elders sacrifice their own power to raise the generation of high generation Laibon...<br /> <br /> <b>The Pursuit of Apotheosis</b> (Level Five ritual of New Age anarchs) also in <i>theory</i> ccould do it\u200b - For every mortal worshiper who dies as part of the ritual, the player must roll one die against a difficulty of 7. Every success gives the player one experience point. From the character\u2019s perspective, these new Attributes, Abilities, and Disciplines are the result of a momentary glimpse of godhood paid for by the deaths of loyal followers. According to some rumors, a sufficient number of successful sacrifices can also be expended to permanently reduce a vampire\u2019s Generation. The truth of those rumors and the number of successes needed to achieve such a feat are left to the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.&quot;<br /> <br /> In <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b> Adonijah gives you a vial containing 5 drops of Malkav's blood.<br /> Drinking a single drop fills your blood pool, heals all your wounds , grants a permanent Willpower point , lowers your Generation by one and finally it cures one Derangement apart from the primary one Malkavians have. - The books states that those particular effects , are not the same effects of every drop of any Antediluvian's vitae. Malkav simply breaks all the rules because , well he is Malkav.<br /> <br /> In <b>Berlin by Night </b>there is Ankla Hotep, who had an amulet crafted for him by a Bane Mummy, his Chimerstry powers increase to the level of an Antediluvian. While using his Chimerstry, he was for all intents and purposes Caine and could alter reality around him within a five-mile radius. Basicallthe amulet grants you Chimerstry 10 and creates a reality bubble. <br /> Just stole this amulet or find the Bane Mummy and convince it to make a similar amulet for you^^<br /> \u200b<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary also have the possibility Enoch is the one who is in the Sarcophagus, if the storyteller want to go that way? Enoch could Embrace someone in to the 3rd Generation<br /> Or if your team like the game of ages, the chronicle could start in the First City... <br /> <br /> In one of the Gehenna scenarios you can get ahold of a vial of Caine\u2019s blood... (It\u2019s mentioned that anyone who tries to drink it explodes but still, exist)<br /> Similarly the Ventrue Antediluvian had a jar filled with Caine's blood according the 1st ed clanbook, hidden in his fortress in the First City with such things like the Claw of Fenris, the Head of Medusa and so on; it is not immposibble to find it...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T11:35:17-07:00","id":1509605,"title":"","content":"There's no official adventure/module type supplement that deals with it to my knowledge. I guess in theory one of the Gehenna paths makes it possible... but it would be rather pointless to do (it's Gehenna after all).<br /> <br /> Is there a reason you're looking for that specific sort of supplement? I think it's pretty understandable, given the impact of a 3rd Generation vampire getting eaten as established in the books, that it's not really been part of general modules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:01:37-07:00","id":1509606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509601-there-is-any-way-raw-to-become-a-3rd-generation-vampire?p=1509605#post1509605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no official adventure/module type supplement that deals with it to my knowledge. I guess in theory one of the Gehenna paths makes it possible... but it would be rather pointless to do (it's Gehenna after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the scenarios has the PCs fight both Tremere and Augustus Giovanni while they're at 3rd gen. Although Tremere suffers from the Withering immediately after regaining his power (probably because of who he chose to eat) and Giovanni is apparently more of a Gem 3.5, so you probably won't get the proper boost up you would in earlier times. But if all you want are the stats...<br /> <br /> <br /> The other reason there's basically no ways to become Gen 3 is because the Antes are plot devices kept as inactive as possible, their rules are literally 'whatever you need'. Blood Pool is indefinitely large, BP/turn is 'whatever they need', and level 10 Disciplines were eventually retconned from actual powers to freeform plot stuff.<br /> <br /> The third reason is, of course, every Ante bar [Ventrue] and Salout has plans to deal with attempted diablerie, and when push came to shove two out of three succeeded. [Ventrue] has no plans because they're the only Ante officially confirmed to have died, whereas Salout seems to have been banking on taking over his diablerist and might have wanted to switch from a Clan of mystics to a Clan of wizards anyway. Trying to eat one is a very bad idea, even if it is very tempting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:24:25-07:00","id":1509609,"title":"","content":"I think they did have stated 3rd generation with Tzmisce on one these sites. But I would take it with a huge grain of salt of it's accuracy and such beings should not be given traits of any sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T13:01:14-07:00","id":1509624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509601-there-is-any-way-raw-to-become-a-3rd-generation-vampire?p=1509605#post1509605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no official adventure/module type supplement that deals with it to my knowledge. I guess in theory one of the Gehenna paths makes it possible... but it would be rather pointless to do (it's Gehenna after all).<br /> <br /> Is there a reason you're looking for that specific sort of supplement? I think it's pretty understandable, given the impact of a 3rd Generation vampire getting eaten as established in the books, that it's not really been part of general modules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure curiosity.<br /> For the most, I don't program to use these ideas in real games.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> So the only official, RAW way, is to reach 4th generation ( playing Diablerie - Mexico or Diablerie - Britain... or both ), then successfully play <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b>\u200b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-25-2023, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T14:58:16-07:00","id":1509631,"title":"","content":"Officially, if a 4th Gen diabs a 3rd Gen, they become a 3rd Gen. There's no inherent need to get more complicated than just cannibalizing your way up the ladder. It's just an extremely dangerous journey with danger that doesn't necessarily end when you finish your ancient blood-god slurpee. Keep in mind some of the older and more powerful 4th Gens have managed to pull off the &quot;possess the vampire that diabed me&quot; trick too.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the RAW for that level of event is very much, &quot;the rules are whatever the ST wants them to be for maximum dramatic effect.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T23:24:16-07:00","id":1509692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509601-there-is-any-way-raw-to-become-a-3rd-generation-vampire?p=1509609#post1509609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they did have stated 3rd generation with Tzmisce on one these sites. But I would take it with a huge grain of salt of it's accuracy and such beings should not be given traits of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Crucible of God&quot; scenario in <i>Gehenna</i> has stats for a vozhd that the Tzimisce antediluvian is manifesting through. They're likely not purely the antediluvian's traits in its own vampiric body though (it probably can't still be said to have one at that point in the story). I think all the physical Attributes, Disciplines, and other traits are those of a standard vozhd, with the mental Attributes, Disciplines, Willpower, etc. of the Eldest Fiend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}